A||||2||Double07||Oil level||||1||
Z||000000||Double07||09-26-2000||06:57 PM||||How do i check the oil level in the tranny, on my 86 Fiero, v6, 4sp?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||09-26-2000||07:50 PM||||Take out the speedo sender(just follow the wires into the tranny) there is a dip stick on the end. Be careful not to knock the gear off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||09-27-2000||11:53 AM||||Double07,<P>Like Phil said you have to remove the speed sensor from the trans.  Looking down at the trans from the driver's side you will see the speed sensor at the rear of the trans.  It will have two wires attached.<P>First clean off any buildup of gunk, oily dirt, etc. from around the sensor so it does not fall into the trans case when you remove the sensor.<P>There is a keeper clip held on by a 10mm (I think) bolt.  The head of this bolt is facing up so you can use a socket on a long extension to easily reach it.  Loosen the bolt (no need to remove it) and rotate the clip so it no longer engages the sensor.  Now the sensor pulls out straight up.  There is an O-ring sealing it to the trans case so wiggle it a bit to loosen it.  BE VERY careful as you pull the sensor out because the plastic speedo gear is attached to the bottom of the sensor and is just slightly smaller than the hole in the trans case.  If you pull and it catches on the trans case the gear could fall off into the trans (not a good thing).<P>Wiggle the sensor slightly to get the gear lined up with the hole so the whole unit comes out.<P>With the sensor out you will see two lines scribed on the sensor shaft housing.  These are the high and low fluid level marks.  Fluid level should be between the marks.<P>Fill the trans with 5W30 motor oil to the proper level through this opening.  If you overfill it oil will blow out of the breather vent and make you think you have blown an axel seal.<P>Insert the sensor back into the hole and wiggle it to seat the O-ring.  Turn it to line up the groove for the keeper clip to engage.  Engage the clip and tighten the bolt.<P>I believe there are some alternate fluids that can be used.  My 85SE manual calls for 5W30 motor oil.  Do not use heavy viscosity differential oil!  This will make the trans shift like cr!p.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
